  "handout": "**What's a D20? What you actually need.**\n\n**The loop, every time:** the DM describes, you say what you try, you roll if it is uncertain, you find out what happened. Then around again.\n\n**Say what you want to happen, not what rule you want to use.** Working out which rule applies is the DM's job.\n\n**A roll is:** what the die says, plus your modifier, against a target only the DM knows. Higher is better.\n\n**Advantage** rolls two d20s and keeps the higher. **Disadvantage** keeps the lower.\n\n**A natural 20 on an attack roll always hits.** It is not automatic success at everything else, whatever you have heard.\n\n**You only roll when the outcome is uncertain and failing would matter.** Most of a session has no dice in it.\n\n**This week:** go to the Discord, say hello, and sign up for Character Creation (A5). You do not need to buy anything.",
